    "user": "U0C4QTL8Z8T",
    "text": "Hi  OLake team, I’m using *OLake v0.11.0* with *Azure Cosmos DB (MongoDB API)* as the source and *GCS via Iceberg* as the destination for my `herely` database.\nBoth source and destination connection tests pass, but sync fails during chunk boundary calculation because OLake still calls `splitVector` even though I configured *Timestamp-based sync*:\n```(CommandNotSupported) Command 'splitVector' not supported```\nI also saw `CursorNotFound` on the `messages` collection.\nIs Azure Cosmos DB MongoDB API fully supported in this setup, and is there any recommended workaround/configuration?",
