  {
    "client_msg_id": "47b6c47c-8cf7-49b5-b6af-0705dba0bc05",
    "type": "message",
    "user": "U08CR7HUWDC",
    "text": "hey \u003c@U0C4QTL8Z8T\u003e,\n\nWe found the issue in the current UI saves *Timestamp* as `\"Timestamp\"`, while the sync expects `\"timestamp\"`. This causes it to fall back to Split Vector, which Cosmos DB doesn’t support. We’ll fix this in the next connector release.\n*Workaround:*\n1. Open DevTools → *Network* and click *Save* on the source.\n2. Find the `PUT` request to `/api/v1/project/\u003cid\u003e/sources/\u003cid\u003e`.\n3. Right-click → *Copy → Copy as cURL*.\n4. Change `\"chunking_strategy\":\"Timestamp\"` to `\"chunking_strategy\":\"timestamp\"` and run the cURL.\n       Example of the edited part:\n```...\\\"backoff_retry_count\\\":3,\\\"chunking_strategy\\\":\\\"timestamp\\\",\\\"```\nThen re-run the sync. *Don’t save the source again from the UI*, as it will change it back to `\"Timestamp\"`.\nPlease let us know if the sync works after this.",
    "ts": "1790588266.917699",
    "thread_ts": "1790583407.242299",
    "edited": {
      "user": "U08CR7HUWDC",
      "ts": "1790592251.000000"
